cartridge "CHIEN DE BERGER/JEAN-FRANCOIS SEHAN/1984"

' CHIEN DE BERGER (the sheepdog) - ColecoVision version of the Oric game by
' Jean-Francois Sehan ("L'Oric a l'affiche", Editions du P.S.I., 1984).
' Adapted by Amy & Claude, Amy Studio 2026. Built by build.py from this file,
' ../_common/amy/core.alexis, pages.txt, art.py and music/*.txt.
'
' THE GAME (as in the book): a fenced meadow, a pen open on its left side,
' the shepherd standing in the way and 5 to 10 sheep. Your sheepdog moves
' around; a sheep steps away from the dog on both axes (one cell at a time;
' same row or column = no move on that axis), bounces off the fence, and does
' not move when the cell is taken. A sheep in the pen only shuffles right and
' never leaves. All the sheep in the pen = the trial is won.
'
' CONTROLS: joystick = the dog runs (4 directions and diagonals); a button =
' bark (sheep further away run too). Title: up/down choose, left/right
' change the starting level, a button confirms.
'
' LIBERTIES (listed for Amy):
' - Real time instead of turns. The book moved the dog freely and then let
'   every sheep, however far, take 5 steps per RETURN, scoring the number of
'   RETURNs. Its model (model/sheepsim.py) shows why that does not survive a
'   joystick: with every sheep fleeing the dog at any distance, even a
'   one-move-ahead search clears a 5-sheep field in 12 tries only ~60% of the
'   time, and a rule-of-thumb player never. Here a sheep only runs from a dog
'   within 3 cells (6 while it barks), one cell every 6 frames; the book's
'   "le plus vite possible" becomes a daylight bar: bring the flock in before
'   the sun sets. Barks replace the tries in the score: fewer = more points.
' - Three dogs (lives); night falls = a dog lost and a new field, same level.
' - Field: columns 3-28, rows 3-20 inside a fence (the Oric's 33 x 22).
'   The pen keeps the book's size (5 x 4 inside, open on the left) and stays
'   two cells off the fence so no sheep can be trapped behind it.
' - A sheep whose diagonal step is blocked tries the straight parts of it,
'   then a side step that does not bring it nearer the dog (the book's
'   sheep froze instead, and a huddle in a corner could stay stuck).
' - Calm sheep sometimes wander one cell; one standing within two cells of
'   the pen's mouth walks in by itself. From level 2, bushes and rocks.
' - Colour, animation, music and sound effects are new; the Oric's PING and
'   SHOOT become the bark and the pen-full jingle.

